&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BYD is the global leader and pioneer in achieving Zero Emission Energy Ecosystem with battery energy storage (ESS), solar power &amp;amp; electrified transportation.&amp;nbsp;BYD’s Energy Storage team provides battery energy storage solutions to strategic customers in the residential, commercial and utility sectors. The team is hiring a Project Manager to support the ESS team rapid growth in North America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB DESCRIPTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the execution of various ESS projects, including but not limited to production, delivery, commissioning, and maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating crucial activities necessary for on-time project delivery within the allocated budget, including technical design, specification compliance, and after-sales support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as the primary point of contact for customers/clients throughout the project execution phase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with the internal engineering, manufacturing, supply chain, and logistics department to facilitate seamless project execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining continuous alignment with high-level company objectives and workflows by collaborating with the Engineering, Procurement, and Business Development teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Updating and maintaining project schedules to ensure accurate tracking of progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting occasional site visits and effectively communicating technical challenges to internal stakeholders, clients, and subcontractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing activity reports and performance data to measure productivity and goal achievement, identifying areas for cost reduction and program improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generating comprehensive reports for company management, highlighting project status, progress, and any relevant issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging with internal and external stakeholders to align project scopes and timelines with realistic goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and manage project payment, ensuring timely payment collection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support contract negotiations, technical due diligence, and streamlining processes to achieve rapid closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring industry trends in clean energy and conducting regular analysis, producing routine presentations to keep stakeholders informed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzing trends in renewable energy system standards and aligning technology strategies accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitating &quot;lessons learned&quot; meetings after project completion to document areas of improvement and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a relevant field (Engineering, Business, Renewable Energy, etc.) or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in project coordination or management, preferably in the solar energy or renewable industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to multitask and prioritize effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, enabling clear and concise interaction with various stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in project scheduling and management tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with clean energy industry trends and technical aspects of solar PV and energy storage systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt to a fast-paced environment and work collaboratively in cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual in Chinese Mandarin and English is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 30% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
